#====================================================================
# E327 - Bound MPICH detached-descendant timeout containment
#====================================================================

id:                     E361
trigger_tool:           conan|mpiexec|hydra
phase:                  test
error_signature:        managed MPI command exceeded [0-9]+ seconds: .*test_process_control.*detach|detached MPI descendant wrote delayed canary for detach

severity:               2
category:               cleanup, mpi, openharmony, process-control, timeout
match_keywords:         MPICH, Hydra, mpiexec, detached descendant, setsid, double fork, managed timeout, zero residue, canary
title:                  Gate detached-descendant canaries on post-cleanup release

root_cause:             A managed MPI launcher may either return while a detached descendant remains or stay live until the bounded harness timeout. The initial timeout acceptance still used a canary written four seconds after startup even though timeout cleanup cannot begin until 15 seconds, so the canary measured pre-cleanup lifetime rather than post-cleanup escape. Substring mode matching also allowed detach to match detach-kill.
affected_scope:         MPI test harnesses that intentionally create double-forked or session-detached descendants and manage the complete launcher tree with PID/starttime/token identity.
verification_cmd:       Execute exact returned-live and timeout positives plus wrong-timeout, wrong-executable, wrong-mode, malformed evidence, survivor, pre/post-gate canary, repeated-gate and unexpected-success negatives; compile and run the C gate harness and prove zero-residue assertion precedes the timeout raise.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           bound-timeout-plus-post-cleanup-token-gate
rec_description:        Keep a finite timeout and parse its command list exactly. Make the child publish an armed token and wait; only after zero-residue cleanup and escape-PID absence may the host create-new the exact release token. Reject any canary before or after that gate, then run a fresh MPI smoke test.
rec_command:            python validate_r65_detached_cleanup_gate.py --conanfile <test_package/conanfile.py> --process-source <test_process_control.c> --scratch <E-drive scratch>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-test-package-managed-mpi

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      returned-live-descendant-path
fallback_description:   Preserve the existing path where mpiexec returns while a tracked descendant remains; clean it by exact process identity and enforce the same postconditions.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       except.*timeout.*pass|managed MPI command exceeded.*return
forbid_1_reason:        A generic timeout does not prove that the intended process-control probe ran or that cleanup completed.
forbid_1_consequence:   Real MPI hangs or foreign residue can be mislabeled as expected containment.

forbid_2_pattern:       outer_timeout\s*=\s*[3-9][0-9]+|sleep\([3-9][0-9]+\)
forbid_2_reason:        Increasing the budget hides the contract mismatch and does not prove descendant containment.
forbid_2_consequence:   Device time is consumed while the same launcher topology remains unresolved.

forbid_3_pattern:       kill.*pid(?!.*start)|terminate.*process(?!.*identity)
forbid_3_reason:        PID-only cleanup is vulnerable to reuse and may affect a foreign process.
forbid_3_consequence:   Cleanup can cross the task ownership boundary.

principles:
